safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#download-limit","content":"Why bandwidth limits matter on remote Sparks"},"256":{"id":"/download-limit-14","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#download-limit","content":"CLI usage (`status`, `run`, `clear`, `wrap`, `--refresh`)"},"257":{"id":"/download-limit-15","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#download-limit","content":"Manual Mbps cap (`download-models --limit N`) vs auto"},"258":{"id":"/download-limit-16","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#download-limit","content":"Auto mode (85% of a duration HTTP / speedtest sample, cached 24h) and wrap lifecycle"},"259":{"id":"/download-limit-17","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#download-limit","content":"**What this enables**"},"260":{"id":"/download-limit-18","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#download-limit","content":"Downloading multi‑GB Klein/Wan/LTX weights without saturating the uplink and freezing SSH"},"261":{"id":"/download-limit-19","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#why","content":"You cannot walk over to a Spark and wiggle the HDMI cable. Bandwidth left for SSH is how you recover a host that is pulling 30 GB of LTX. A full-rate Hugging Face pull can starve interactive SSH. This utility applies kernel-level traffic shaping via **wondershaper** when HTB is available, and falls back to gentler HF client settings when it is not. Wrap **always clears on exit** — do not weaken that."},"262":{"id":"/download-limit-20","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#why","content":"Inspired by the throttled Ollama downloader in `dgx-spark-it-up`, generalized and improved with **auto** limiting."},"263":{"id":"/download-limit-21","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"Command"},"264":{"id":"/download-limit-22","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"Purpose"},"265":{"id":"/download-limit-23","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"`status [--json] [--refresh]`"},"266":{"id":"/download-limit-24","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"Report interface + speed cache; `--refresh` remasures"},"267":{"id":"/download-limit-25","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"`run --limit 50`"},"268":{"id":"/download-limit-26","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"Apply a fixed Mbps cap"},"269":{"id":"/download-limit-27","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"`run --limit auto`"},"270":{"id":"/download-limit-28","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"Measure line rate (or cache), apply 85%"},"271":{"id":"/download-limit-29","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"`clear`"},"272":{"id":"/download-limit-30","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"Remove wondershaper limit (does **not** drop the speed cache)"},"273":{"id":"/download-limit-31","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"`wrap --limit auto` or `--limit N`"},"274":{"id":"/download-limit-32","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"Apply → run command → **always clear on exit**"},"275":{"id":"/download-limit-33","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"`manage.sh download-models --limit N`"},"276":{"id":"/download-limit-34","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"Same wrap; **N** is a standing Mbps cap for this download"},"277":{"id":"/download-limit-35","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"Via manage:"},"278":{"id":"/download-limit-36","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"`--limit N` is integer **Mbps** (not MB/s). 40 Mbps ≈ 5 MB/s. `.env` `DOWNLOAD_LIMIT=40` is the persistent default; the flag wins for one invocation. Wrap still **clears on exit**. `--limit` is not `--tier` — pack ids live on Download tiers."},"279":{"id":"/download-limit-37","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"When you pass `--limit auto`:"},"280":{"id":"/download-limit-38","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"**Cache** — reuse a host-local measurement from the last 24h (`${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/ez-comfy/download-limit-speed.json`). Not stored on `MODELS_DIR` (independent Sparks share that). `--refresh` or `DOWNLOAD_LIMIT_CACHE_TTL_SEC=0` skips the cache."},"281":{"id":"/download-limit-39","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"**Clear** any existing bandwidth limits on the default-route interface (wondershaper + best-effort `tc`) so residual caps do not skew a new sample"},"282":{"id":"/download-limit-40","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"**Duration HTTP probe** first: large Cloudflare `__down?bytes=` payload (default 250 MB) with `--max-time` \\~12s. curl **timeout (exit 28) is a valid sample** when ≥1 MB arrived — a short completed file under-reads gigabit (TCP slow start)"},"283":{"id":"/download-limit-41","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"Else Ookla `speedtest` JSON if on PATH (take **max** vs HTTP when both succeed)"},"284":{"id":"/download-limit-42","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"Else install and try `speedtest-cli --simple` (often under-reads gigabit; last resort)"},"285":{"id":"/download-limit-43","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"Apply `floor(0.85 × measured)` (minimum 1 Mbps) when the sample is **trusted**, and **write the cache**"},"286":{"id":"/download-limit-44","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"If all probes fail: **do not** use idle NIC RX as line rate — use default `max-workers=4` and start download. Fallback `DOWNLOAD_LIMIT_FALLBACK` is **not** cached"},"287":{"id":"/download-limit-45","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"++ctrl+c++ kills the download process group, progress heartbeat, and HTTP probes (INT→TERM→KILL)."},"288":{"id":"/download-limit-46","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"Override HTTP probe: `SPEEDTEST_HTTP_URL`, `SPEEDTEST_HTTP_BYTES`, `SPEEDTEST_HTTP_MAX_TIME`."},"289":{"id":"/download-limit-47","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"Upload is set to a high **legal** “uncapped” rate (clamped for HTB). Extremely large historical defaults (e.g. 100000 Mbps) produced `Illegal \"rate\"` on some kernels."},"290":{"id":"/download-limit-48","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#dgx-spark--no-htb","content":"Many Spark kernels lack `sch_htb` / IFB (`qdisc kind is unknown`). The tool **detects** this and **does not** spam wondershaper/RTNETLINK."},"291":{"id":"/download-limit-49","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#dgx-spark--no-htb","content":"Path"},"292":{"id":"/download-limit-50","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","won